# The daily learning loop: a headless Claude Code run that writes the journal.
# Read by scripts/gen_launchd.py.

[job]
name = learning
exit_timeout = 1800
run_at_load = false
stdin = {ROOT}/config/prompts/daily_learning_loop.md

[program]
{CLAUDE}
-p
--permission-mode
acceptEdits
--allowedTools
Read Glob Grep Write Edit Bash(git add:*) Bash(git commit:*) Bash(git status:*) Bash(git diff:*) Bash(git log:*)

[environment]
TZ = America/New_York
PATH = {HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin
HOME = {HOME}
AGENTIC_TRADING_ROOT = {ROOT}

[schedule]
# 4:30 PM Eastern, after the close, every weekday.
at 16:30 on weekdays

[comment]
The daily learning loop, run by launchd.

At 16:30 Eastern on weekdays it starts Claude Code with no terminal attached and
feeds it the prompt at {ROOT}/config/prompts/daily_learning_loop.md on standard
input. Claude reads the day's tick log, the five book state files, the watchdog
and alert logs, the pre-flight result and the day's commits, and writes one
journal entry at {ROOT}/journal/YYYY-MM-DD.md plus the five line
{ROOT}/journal/latest_summary.md that the hub relays to Mo.

Confirmed learnings graduate to {ROOT}/docs/LEARNINGS.md and improvements go to
{ROOT}/docs/BACKLOG.md. The rules for all of that are in the prompt file, not
here, so changing what the loop does is an edit to the prompt.

WHAT IT IS ALLOWED TO DO. Reading, writing files, and a short list of git
commands. The allowed tools list above is the whole of it. It cannot run the
trading loop, cannot reach IB Gateway or the MCP server, and cannot place an
order. The prompt says the same thing in words.

WHAT IT NEEDS. Claude Code installed and signed in as Mo on this Mac, and the
Mac logged in to the desktop, because a user launchd job runs in the login
session and Claude reads its sign in from the login keychain. A locked screen is
fine. A logged out Mac is not.

If nothing appears in {ROOT}/journal/ after 16:30, read
{ROOT}/output/launchd_learning.err.log first. A sign in that has expired shows up
there.
